steps.message:
In this test:
```python
    Item = Annotated[
        Union[Annotated[FirstItem, Tag("first")], Annotated[OtherItem, Tag("other")]],
        Field(discriminator="value"),
    ]

    @app.post("/items/")
    def save_union_body_discriminator(
        item: Item, q: Annotated[str, Field(description="Query string")]
    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:
        return {"item": item}
```
`item` is `Item`, which is `Annotated[Union[...], Field(discriminator="value")]`.
And it's used as a parameter in a POST request, so FastAPI implicitly treats it as `Body()`.

The issue says "inside of `Annotated` with `Body()`".
So maybe:
```python
    @app.post("/items/")
    def save_union_body_discriminator(
        item: Annotated[Item, Body()], q: Annotated[str, Field(description="Query string")]
    ) -> Dict[str, Any]:
        return {"item": item}
```
where `Item` is already `Annotated[Union[...], Field(discriminator="value")]`.

Wait, if I do `Annotated[Item, Body()]`, and `Item` is `Annotated[Union[...], Field(discriminator="value")]`, then I have nested `Annotated`.

Let's try to reproduce this specific case.

